<div id="europe" v-cloak>
  <div purpose="page-container">
    <div purpose="page-content">

      <div purpose="page-hero">
        <div purpose="page-heading">
          <h4>Device management for Europe</h4>
          <h1>Keep device data in the EU</h1>
        </div>
        <div purpose="hero-text">
          <p>Your devices, your data. Manage Windows, macOS, Linux, and mobile devices from one independent platform.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="hero-badges">
          <div purpose="hero-badge">
            <img alt="ISO/IEC 27001 certified" src="/images/europe-iso-27001-64x64@2x.png">
            <p>ISO/IEC 27001<br>certified</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="hero-badge">
            <img alt="GDPR compliant" src="/images/europe-gdpr-compliant-48x48@2x.png">
            <p>GDPR compliant</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="button-row">
          <a purpose="cta-button" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
          <animated-arrow-button href="/case-study/mollie">Read the case study</animated-arrow-button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading">
          <div>
            <h4>Data sovereignty</h4>
            <h2>Keep device data in Europe</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Choose where Fleet runs and what it collects, without losing features. No forced cloud services or hidden dependencies.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="hosting-options">
          <div purpose="hosting-option">
            <%# <img alt="Hosted in Europe" src="TODO"> %>
            <h5>Hosted in Europe</h5>
            <p>Fully managed, with your instance and its device data hosted in the European Union.</p>
            <div purpose="tags">
              <span purpose="tag">EU region</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="hosting-option">
            <%# <img alt="Your EU cloud" src="TODO"> %>
            <h5>Your EU cloud</h5>
            <p>Run Fleet in your own account, in an EU region, or with a European provider you already trust.</p>
            <div purpose="tags">
              <span purpose="tag">Your account</span>
              <span purpose="tag">Your keys</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="hosting-option">
            <%# <img alt="On-premises" src="TODO"> %>
            <h5>On-premises</h5>
            <p>Your data center, your hardware, your network boundary. Fleet runs on bare metal or VMs.</p>
            <div purpose="tags">
              <span purpose="tag">Bare metal</span>
              <span purpose="tag">VMs</span>
              <span purpose="tag">Kubernetes</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="hosting-option">
            <%# <img alt="Air-gapped" src="TODO"> %>
            <h5>Air-gapped</h5>
            <p>For defense, critical infrastructure, and classified networks, where nothing leaves the building.</p>
            <div purpose="tags">
              <span purpose="tag">No outbound connection</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-with-image">
        <div purpose="feature-image">
          <img alt="Annex III of the EU AI Act is required by December 2, 2027" src="/images/eu-ai-act-annex-iii-800x600@2x.png">
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-text">
          <h2>Annex III of the EU AI Act is required by December 2, 2027</h2>
          <p>To put AI to work in Europe, you need to be able to know what AI employees are using. Fleet finds AI coding tools, IDE plugins, MCP servers, and AI skills that developers install on their own and give AI agents running on employee systems access to files and systems.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-with-image" class="reverse">
        <div purpose="feature-image">
          <img alt="Device data shown to employees in Fleet Desktop" src="/images/mdm-scope-transparency-800x600@2x.png">
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-text">
          <h2>Show your works council exactly what Fleet sees</h2>
          <p>In Germany, the Netherlands, France, and beyond, employee representatives often have a say over software that could monitor staff. Fleet makes that review shorter because there's nothing hidden to explain.</p>
          <div purpose="checklist">
            <p>Employees <a href="/better">see the same</a> device data IT sees</p>
            <p>Support multiple countries and data collection rules, so each works council can match its own agreement</p>
            <p>Labour councils can see which policies have changed</p>
          </div>
          <p purpose="feature-note">Fleet doesn't replace a works agreement. It makes one easier to write and easier to verify.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="feature-with-image">
        <div purpose="feature-image">
          <img alt="Windows configuration profiles in Fleet" src="/images/feature-profile-generation-504x378@2x.png">
        </div>
        <div purpose="feature-text">
          <h2>Manage and patch Windows without buying two products</h2>
          <p>Build Windows profiles without Intune, patch apps in the same place, and show auditors the results. Your PCs run on the same platform as your Macs and Linux devices.</p>
          <div purpose="checklist">
            <p>Build and apply Windows profiles directly, with no extra Microsoft server in between.</p>
            <p>Patch when the app is closed, or force the update for critical fixes.</p>
          </div>
          <div purpose="stats">
            <div purpose="stat">
              <h3>1400+</h3>
              <p>Fleet-maintained apps across macOS and Windows, with nothing to manage.</p>
            </div>
            <div purpose="stat">
              <h3>Hourly</h3>
              <p>Patch policies move to the latest version on their own.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="quote-and-logos">
        <div purpose="section-quote">
          <div purpose="quote-author-image">
            <img alt="Mason Peressini" src="/images/mason-peressini-120x120@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="quote-content">
            <p purpose="quote-text">“I'm spending about 20 hours a week less on managing PCs than I was with Intune.”</p>
            <div purpose="name-and-title">
              <p purpose="author-name">Mason Peressini</p>
              <p purpose="author-title">Sr Systems Support Specialist</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="logo-grid">
          <div purpose="logo"><img alt="Mollie logo" src="/images/mollie-logo-136x40@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img alt="Proton logo" src="/images/logos/logo-proton-color-79x20@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img alt="Starling Bank logo" src="/images/logos/logo-starling-bank-color-80x24@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img alt="Vector logo" src="/images/logos/logo-vector-color-86x24@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img alt="Legora logo" src="/images/logos/logo-legora-color-83x24@2x.png"></div>
          <div purpose="logo"><img alt="SUSE logo" src="/images/logos/logo-suse-color-58x12@2x.png"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="page-section">
        <div purpose="section-heading" class="left-aligned">
          <h2>Built for Europe</h2>
          <p>Fleet's security program and privacy are independently audited and published in the open. Your procurement team, security team, labour councils, and data protection officer can check it any time.</p>
        </div>
        <div purpose="compliance-cards">
          <div purpose="compliance-card">
            <img alt="ISO/IEC 27001 certified" src="/images/europe-iso-27001-64x64@2x.png">
            <h5>ISO/IEC 27001 certified</h5>
            <p>Fleet's information security management system is independently certified against the same standard your ISMS follows.</p>
            <div purpose="helps-you-meet">
              <p>Helps you meet</p>
              <div purpose="tags">
                <span purpose="tag">ISO A.5.19–5.22</span>
                <span purpose="tag">NIS2 Art. 21(2)(d)</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="compliance-card">
            <img alt="GDPR compliant" src="/images/europe-gdpr-compliant-48x48@2x.png">
            <h5>GDPR compliant</h5>
            <p>Fleet processes personal data under a data processing agreement, with a published sub-processor list.</p>
            <div purpose="helps-you-meet">
              <p>Helps you meet</p>
              <div purpose="tags">
                <span purpose="tag">GDPR Art. 28</span>
                <span purpose="tag">Data residency</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div purpose="compliance-card">
            <img alt="SOC 2 audited" src="/images/europe-soc-2-audited-64x64@2x.png">
            <h5>SOC 2 audited</h5>
            <p>An independent audit of Fleet's security controls, for vendor reviews that ask for both ISO and SOC 2.</p>
            <div purpose="helps-you-meet">
              <p>Helps you meet</p>
              <div purpose="tags">
                <span purpose="tag">DORA Art. 28</span>
                <span purpose="tag">Vendor questionnaires</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div purpose="trust-cards">
          <div purpose="trust-card">
            <div purpose="trust-card-text">
              <h5>trust.fleetdm.com</h5>
              <p>Live control status, security policies, and penetration test results.</p>
            </div>
            <a purpose="cta-button" href="https://trust.fleetdm.com" target="_blank" no-icon>Visit trust center</a>
          </div>
          <div purpose="trust-card">
            <div purpose="trust-card-text">
              <h5>Open source, top to bottom</h5>
              <p>The agent, server, and CLI are public on GitHub, so your security team can audit the code itself.</p>
            </div>
            <animated-arrow-button href="https://github.com/fleetdm/fleet" target="_blank" no-icon>View on GitHub</animated-arrow-button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="quote-section">
        <div purpose="quote-image">
          <img alt="Mollie logo" src="/images/mollie-logo-136x40@2x.png">
        </div>
        <p purpose="quote-text">“When a tool touches every device in our environment, security and residency is non-negotiable. Fleet's ISO 27001 certification, combined with their open-source transparency, means we can see exactly how the product works and trust how our data is protected.”</p>
        <div purpose="quote-author-info">
          <div purpose="quote-author-image">
            <img alt="Sam Clark" src="/images/sam-clark-120x120@2x.png">
          </div>
          <div purpose="name-and-title">
            <p purpose="author-name">Sam Clark</p>
            <p purpose="author-title">Infrastructure Manager</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div purpose="bottom-cta">
        <div purpose="page-heading">
          <h4>Device management for Europe</h4>
          <h1>Your devices, your data, your independence</h1>
        </div>
        <div purpose="button-row">
          <a purpose="cta-button" href="/contact?talkToUs">Get a demo</a>
          <animated-arrow-button href="/pricing">Compare features</animated-arrow-button>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
  <cloud-city></cloud-city>
</div>
<%- /* Expose server-rendered data as window.SAILS_LOCALS :: */ exposeLocalsToBrowser() %>
